      "description": "The Mataram Kotagede Gedhe Mosque is one of the oldest mosques in existence\nin the Yogyakarta area, and is a mosque heritage of the Mataram Kingdom. In\nIn the Kotagede area of ​​Yogyakarta, there are still historical relics that save\ninformation about the Mataram Kingdom. One of the historical places in Kotagede is\nThe Mataram Gedhe Mosque which was built during the Mataram Kingdom era in\n1640. The Great Mosque of Mataram was built by Sultan Agung who worked together\n\nwith people who still adhere to Hinduism and Buddhism.",
